  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of Pre-Inca and Inca Textiles and Metal and Other Objects in the Samuel Humberto Espinoza Lozano Archaeological Museum</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Located along the Vilcashuamn-Pisco section of the Qhapaq an (Inca Road), the archaeological site and historic town of Huaytar are important cultural tourism destinations in the central Andes. This project includes the conservation for eventual display of 50 of the museums finest textiles and other objects.</narrative>
  </description>
